b.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16ffx.jpg"}, {"id": 1979568, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16fg0.jpg"}, {"id": 1979569, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16fg1.jpg"}, {"id": 1979566, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16ffy.jpg"}, {"id": 1979567, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16ffz.jpg"}], "slug": "arcade-archives-2-elevator-action", "summary": "\"ELEVATOR ACTION\" is an action game released by TAITO in 1983. As a Spy, your goal is to infiltrate the building and escape with all the confidential documents. Use elevators to crush enemies, attack them by shooting down lamps, and more.\n\nThe \u201cArcade Archives\u201d series is developed with the concept of faithfully reproducing classic arcade games. It also includes convenient features such as difficulty and screen settings, rewind, rapid-fire, and multiple save slots. In addition, players can compete for the best scores with players around the world through online rankings.\n\u201cArcade Archives 2\u201d adds a new \u201cTIME ATTACK MODE\u201d to the lineup of \u201cORIGINAL MODE,\u201d \u201cHI SCORE MODE,\u201d and \u201cCARAVAN MODE\u201d included in the Arcade Archives series. In \u201cTIME ATTACK MODE,\u201d players compete to clear the game as quickly as possible, regardless of the score achieved. VRR (Variable Refresh Rate) support has also been added, allowing gameplay to be reproduced even closer to the original arcade experience.", "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/arcade-archives-2-elevator-action"}